.TH ICINGA2-SPLUNK-CHECK 1 "November 2026" "icinga2-splunk" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
icinga2-splunk-check \- check connectivity to Icinga2 and Splunk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B icinga2-splunk-check
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validates the configuration, then checks that the Icinga2 API and its event
stream accept the credentials and that Splunk HEC accepts the token. Nothing
is indexed in Splunk. Run it as the service user before enabling the service:
.PP
.RS
sudo \-u icinga2-splunk icinga2-splunk-check
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Configuration file (default: \fI/etc/icinga2-splunk/splunk_config.json\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if all checks pass, 1 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR icinga2-splunk (1)
